{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRySppVyb1ymQkYjhaJt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added all six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` to the registration and offers screens, using `Analytics.capture` with the exact names and properties. I didn't compile or run anything, so the code is untested.\n\n- **Email and phone started:** these fire on the first edit of each field per screen visit. A text field's `onChanged` runs on every keystroke, so a once-only flag keeps it to one event. No email or phone value is sent.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** this fires when the user lets go of the slider, with `amount`. One drag sends one event instead of one per step.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** this fires when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** this fires on the Continue tap, with `amount` and `terms`, just before navigating to the offers screen.\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** this fires each time a scroll finishes, with `offset`. A user who scrolls many times sends many events. If that's too many for your event quota, a once-per-visit flag would cap it.\n\nThe colleague's note was about analytics events that fire on every keystroke, slider step or scroll update and use up the free quota. That applies here, so I used its once-only flag, slider-release and scroll-end fixes. I didn't use its focus-lost approach, because no event needs the field's final value. I also didn't do its debug-log check, since there was no build.\n\n`ANSWER.md` records what I did and which parts of the note applied."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2128,"cache_read_input_tokens":24321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2128},"output_tokens":478,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostic